    "type": "question",
    "label": "3",
    "prompt": "Consider rotations of $90^\\circ$, $180^\\circ$ or $270^\\circ$, clockwise or anticlockwise, about a centre $O$. Are any points fixed under these rotations, or do they all move?",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "Only the centre of rotation, $O$, is fixed.",
      "worked": "Each of these rotations is a nonidentity rotation about $O$. The centre $O$ stays in the same position; every other point moves.",
